  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">A ledger is a record of <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-transaction-in-crypto\"><strong id=\"\">transactions</strong></a>. The “state” of a ledger can be derived by adding up all the transactions from the very start of the ledger to the present time.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-transaction-in-crypto\"><strong id=\"\">What is a “transaction” in crypto?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">What are the Radix Public Network and Radix Ledger?</strong></a></li></ul>",
